WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.671
- [Narrator] OK, Cree,
whenever you're ready.

00:00:02.671 --> 00:00:05.255
- I'll hug you and
squeeze you and kiss you

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:07.271
and put coins in your eyes.

00:00:07.271 --> 00:00:11.463
That's why we gonna be
kids next door forever.

00:00:11.463 --> 00:00:13.560
I am Kidagakash.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.711
Welcome to the City of Atlantis.

00:00:16.711 --> 00:00:19.896
Angelica, you know that
you're mean to those babies,

00:00:19.896 --> 00:00:21.214
and I've had enough!

00:00:21.214 --> 00:00:23.988
I will not let you bother
them again. (banner swishes)

00:00:23.988 --> 00:00:25.208
- [Narrator] Works for me.

00:00:25.208 --> 00:00:28.294
(energetic, percussive music)

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.877
(steady, percussive music)

00:00:33.342 --> 00:00:37.272
This is Cree Summer, and her
voice is kind of legendary.

00:00:37.272 --> 00:00:41.605
- I am best known for being
Penny from Inspector Gadget.

00:00:41.605 --> 00:00:44.088
Follow them, Brain, they look suspicious.

00:00:44.088 --> 00:00:46.127
Inspector Gadget, are you alright?

00:00:46.127 --> 00:00:51.127
Susie Carmichael, who
really stood up to Angelica

00:00:51.326 --> 00:00:53.319
and took care of those babies.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:57.971
And I play Elmyra (sings off-key).

00:00:57.971 --> 00:01:01.511
Princess Kida from the
lost city of Atlantis.

00:01:01.511 --> 00:01:03.958
Loh-gee-goh-neh.

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:07.351
(laughs) There you go.

00:01:07.351 --> 00:01:10.351
There's the taste of some
of my greatest hits. (claps)

00:01:10.351 --> 00:01:13.054
- I knew Uncle Gadget
would never rob a bank.

00:01:13.054 --> 00:01:16.615
- Let's see, I started voice
acting when I was 11 years old.

00:01:16.615 --> 00:01:19.590
My father, Don Francks,
was the voice of Sabretooth

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.423
from the "X-Men."

00:01:20.423 --> 00:01:23.102
He also was the very first
person to every voice Boba Fett

00:01:23.102 --> 00:01:25.799
from "Star Wars," which
is such a cool-ass thing.

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:28.335
And he had already been
cast on "Inspector Gadget."

00:01:28.335 --> 00:01:31.678
And he asked if they would
be kind enough to read his

00:01:31.678 --> 00:01:34.735
daughter, and they said,
"Sure, we'll give her a shot".

00:01:34.735 --> 00:01:37.726
And it literally took off
like wildfire from there.

00:01:37.726 --> 00:01:40.166
- Hi, my name's Susie, what's yours?

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:43.047
- I know for Susie, one of
the most important things was

00:01:43.047 --> 00:01:46.424
that she sound smart and
that she's very well spoken

00:01:46.424 --> 00:01:50.255
because there were not a lot
of brown girls in cartoons.

00:01:50.255 --> 00:01:52.263
As a matter of fact, there still aren't.

00:01:52.263 --> 00:01:54.343
- [Narrator] Beyond all
this, Cree is unique

00:01:54.343 --> 00:01:55.416
for another reason.

00:01:55.416 --> 00:01:58.398
Historically, white voice
actors generally did the voices

00:01:58.398 --> 00:02:00.879
for cartoon characters of all races.

00:02:00.879 --> 00:02:04.190
Cree has thrived in space that
has often overlooked people

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.118
who look like her.

00:02:05.118 --> 00:02:05.951
- Ow!

00:02:05.951 --> 00:02:07.919
Come on in, boys.

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:10.014
I just put on some moth balls.

00:02:10.014 --> 00:02:11.157
(playful string music)

00:02:11.157 --> 00:02:12.265
(remote clicks)

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:15.439
- What if some talent agent
comes along and says I have--

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:16.303
- I mean, let's face it.

00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:18.351
I do the voices of all the brown girls.

00:02:18.351 --> 00:02:20.295
And all the animated brown girls ...

00:02:20.295 --> 00:02:22.119
there still ain't that many

00:02:22.119 --> 00:02:24.943
because there's this really
crazy belief that black girls

00:02:24.943 --> 00:02:27.975
don't watch cartoons, and
that we don't collect comics,

00:02:27.975 --> 00:02:31.311
and that we don't like
Sci-Fi, and that's B.S., man.

00:02:31.311 --> 00:02:32.551
We love it.

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:35.704
I love when people of color
come up to me and say,

00:02:35.704 --> 00:02:37.566
"You don't know what it
meant to me to see myself

00:02:37.566 --> 00:02:38.488
in a cartoon.

00:02:38.488 --> 00:02:40.734
"I got one little black
girl that I get to see

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:41.623
that looks like me.

00:02:41.623 --> 00:02:43.023
"Thank you so much."

00:02:43.023 --> 00:02:45.356
I get off on that. It's great.

00:02:46.946 --> 00:02:49.363
(icon dings)

